<!--
The blog listing, generated from each post's frontmatter rather than maintained
by hand: <RouteIndex/> lists this route's children, ordered by the number their
filenames carry and reversed so the newest reads first. A post's title,
description, author and date all come from its own `+++` block, so adding a post
is adding a file.

The `{PageMeta{..}}` spread is a ROOT DECLARATION, what frontmatter is in a
markdown page: document metadata as a component, read off this file by the
`<RoutesDir/>` scan without building it (so the nav knows this page before anyone
visits it) and hoisted onto the rendered page as well (so the document title
binds to it).

The heading is hand-authored because this page is undated: `<ArticleHeader/>` in
the shared `ArticleLayout` gates on `created`, so it renders for every post and
not for this index.
-->
<Fragment {PageMeta{title: "The Full Moon Harvest", sidebar_label: "Blog", order: 1, expanded: true}}>
	<h1>The Full Moon Harvest</h1>
	<RouteIndex reverse="true"/>
</Fragment>
